Extropians,

If I were in the boonies where bear or other dangerous animals
were a threat, I would carry a .357 or .45 caliber handgun in a
holster on my belt.  Contrary to the opinion expressed in the
original post, it is possible to bring a handgun into play
extremely quickly.  While a rifle has MUCH more stopping power,
it is cumbersome and impractical where threats are unlikely and
response time is short.  As in any confrontation with a dangerous
opponent, though, the outcome is always problematical.  A .22
*might* do the trick, but even a bazooka wouldn't necessarily be
a sure thing.  Such is the nature of life.

One thing that will NOT work on anything but humans (and not even
on them particularly well) is Mace.  It would not even faze a
bear.  Pepper sprays might work a little better, but I doubt it.
Personal chemical defense weapons are a joke.

I doubt noise and light makers would do much good.  But if they
were effective at all, the pistol would still be better.  Guns
are *great* noise and light makers (as well a terrific projectile
slinger).

