Tuesday is that if it were *easier* to obtain a carrying permit on Long Island, 
the killer wouldn't have done nearly as much damage, or, more likely, would not 
have ever boarded the train to begin with.  Having been an LIRR passenger for 
many years, I can assure you that at least one commuter in each car of that 
train would have been packing heat.  Of course, the assholes who run our 
government are reacting in just the opposite way; they're taking an isolated 
event and turning the killer into a poster-boy for (even more) gun control.  

